            "level": {
                "value": 7
            },
            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>With their nocturnal habits, taste for blood, and proclivity for haunting towns and graveyards in the dead of night, it's unsurprising that sangois are often mistaken for vampires. These smaller fey hunt by following the sounds of their victims' hearts, preferring humanoid victims but settling for animal blood if necessary. They wear roughly cut animal hides to stay warm and are often mistaken for prowling coyotes or wildcats when glimpsed from a window on a cold, misty night.</p>",
